``doctor`` is a read-only preflight, while ``build`` and ``image`` print
deterministic dry-run plans.  The deliberately narrow ``test-smoke`` runner
owns the state-changing Phase 0 flow; ``measure-smoke`` only orchestrates that
runner. Both execute only as root inside Linux/WSL, use fixed virtual-artifact
paths, and never accept a host disk as input.
"""

